  <WorldInfo title='Shroud of Turin: spectral and perception laboratory' info='&quot;Albedo = lerp(LUT row h=0, LUT row h=1, h) under a chosen illuminant (data/spectral), or the JJE reflectance at one wavelength.&quot; &quot;Per fragment, the image is filtered by the dissolve model (data/perception.json): it fades below about 1.8 m.&quot; &quot;The weave normal map repeats at Vial&apos;s counts: 38.3 warp and 25.4 weft threads per cm.&quot; &quot;gain multiplies the image contrast for display only (1 = physical). Body image: a synthetic forward model.&quot;'>
